<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/aix-galericulata> bird:account "A small duck of wooded rivers and lakes in East Asia. The male has orange 'sails' on the back, orange whiskers and a red bill. It nests in holes in trees, and the ducklings jump from the nest to the ground soon after they hatch. Feral populations live in Britain and other parts of Europe."@en ;
