<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/anarhynchus> bird:habitat <https://example.org/birds/vocab/habitat/riverine> .

<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/anarhynchus-bicinctus> bird:account "A small plover of beaches and riverbeds. In the breeding season the adult has a narrow black band across the neck and a broad chestnut band across the breast. It breeds throughout New Zealand. After breeding, many birds from the South Island cross the Tasman Sea to winter in south-eastern Australia, which makes it a rare east-to-west migrant across that sea."@en ;
