<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/antigone-canadensis> bird:account "A tall grey crane with a red crown. In March, more than half a million birds gather on the Platte River in Nebraska, where they roost in shallow channels and feed on waste corn before they fly north to breed in Canada, Alaska and Siberia. It was formerly placed in the genus Grus."@en ;
