<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/ardenna-grisea> bird:account "A dark, slender shearwater with silvery underwings. It breeds in burrows on islands around southern New Zealand, where Rakiura Māori harvest the chicks as tītī. After breeding, birds make a figure-of-eight migration around the Pacific Ocean, to the waters off Japan, Alaska and California, and return in the southern spring."@en ;
