<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/arenaria-interpres> bird:account "A stocky, short-legged wader with a short wedge-shaped bill and harlequin black, white and chestnut plumage in summer. It turns over stones, seaweed and shells to find food. It breeds in the Arctic and winters on coasts on every continent except Antarctica."@en ;
