<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/balearica-regulorum> bird:account "A grey crane with a crown of stiff golden feathers, white cheeks and a red throat pouch. It is the only crane that roosts in trees. Pairs dance, bow and boom in the wet season. It lives in wetlands and grassland of eastern and southern Africa, where the drainage of wetlands has caused its decline."@en ;
