<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/bubo-scandiacus> bird:account "A large white owl of the Arctic tundra. Males are almost pure white, and females have dark bars. It hunts in daylight in the Arctic summer, mainly lemmings. In years when lemmings are few, birds move far south in winter. It was formerly placed in its own genus, Nyctea."@en ;
