<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/bucorvus-leadbeateri> bird:account "A very large, black, turkey-like hornbill with a red face and throat. Groups walk through grassland and savanna in search of insects, reptiles, frogs and small mammals. Their deep booming calls carry for several kilometres at dawn. A pair raises only one chick every few years, with help from other members of the group."@en ;
