<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/cacatua-galerita> bird:account "A large white cockatoo with a yellow crest that it raises when alarmed or excited. Flocks feed on seeds, roots and fruit, and post sentinels in trees that screech an alarm. In Sydney, birds have learned to open the lids of wheelie bins, and the skill has spread from suburb to suburb by social learning."@en ;
