<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/calidris-acuminata> bird:account "A medium-sized sandpiper with a rufous cap and a chestnut tint to the breast. It breeds in north-eastern Siberia and is one of the most common migratory waders on freshwater and coastal wetlands of Australia from September to April. Unlike most waders it often feeds on inland wetlands and flooded grassland."@en ;
