<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/calidris-tenuirostris> bird:account "A large, grey sandpiper with heavy dark spotting on the breast in breeding plumage. It breeds in the mountains of north-eastern Siberia and spends the non-breeding season mostly in northern Australia. Almost the whole population stops in the Yellow Sea on migration, so the loss of tidal flats at Saemangeum in Korea caused a sharp fall in numbers."@en ;
