<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/circus-approximans> bird:account "A large brown hawk that glides slowly low over open country and wetlands, with its wings held in a shallow V. It eats small mammals, birds, frogs, insects and carrion, and is often seen at roadkill. Old birds are pale, almost cream, below. It is common in New Zealand, Australia and many Pacific islands."@en ;
