<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/cyanistes-caeruleus> bird:account "A small, agile tit with a blue cap, wings and tail, a yellow breast and a white face with a dark eye-stripe. It hangs upside down to take insects from twigs. It nests in holes and nest boxes, and times its large brood so that the chicks hatch when caterpillars are most abundant on the oaks."@en ;
