<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/cyanocitta-cristata> bird:account "A crested blue jay with black and white markings and a loud, varied voice. It also imitates the call of the red-shouldered hawk. It stores acorns in the ground in autumn and is thought to have helped oaks spread north after the last ice age."@en ;
