<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/dolichonyx-oryzivorus> bird:account "A blackbird of hayfields. The breeding male is black below and buff and white above, the reverse of most birds. It breeds in North America and winters in the grasslands of South America, a round trip of about 20,000 km. It finds its way partly by the earth's magnetic field."@en ;
