<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/falco-amurensis> bird:account "A small falcon. The male is dark grey with rufous thighs and white underwings, and both sexes have red legs and a red ring around the eye. It breeds in eastern Asia and makes one of the longest migrations of any bird of prey: across India and then the Arabian Sea to southern Africa, where flocks roost in towns."@en ;
