<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/fratercula-arctica> bird:account "A small auk with a large, striped red, yellow and blue-grey bill in the breeding season. It nests in burrows on grassy cliff tops in the North Atlantic, and carries rows of sand eels crosswise in its bill to its chick. It spends the winter far out at sea, and loses the bright plates of its bill."@en ;
