<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/gymnorhina-tibicen> bird:account "A black and white bird of open country and towns across Australia and southern New Guinea, with a rich, flute-like carolling song. Groups defend territories all year. In spring a small number of males swoop at people who come near their nest. It feeds on the ground, mostly on insects and their larvae."@en ;
