<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/haematopus-finschi> bird:account "A black and white oystercatcher with a long orange-red bill. It breeds inland on South Island riverbeds and farmland in spring, then moves to northern harbours for the rest of the year. It uses its bill to open shellfish and to probe for worms. Its numbers increased greatly in the twentieth century."@en ;
