<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/haliaeetus-leucocephalus> bird:account "A large eagle with a white head and tail and a heavy yellow bill, the national bird of the United States. It catches fish and also steals them from ospreys. DDT reduced it to about 400 pairs in the lower 48 states in the 1960s. After DDT was banned, the population recovered, and it left the endangered species list in 2007."@en ;
