<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/hemiphaga-novaeseelandiae> bird:account "A large pigeon with an iridescent green and purple head and a clean white breast. Its wingbeats make a loud whooshing sound. It is the only bird left in New Zealand that can swallow the large fruits of trees such as taraire and tawa, so it is important for the spread of their seeds."@en ;
