<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/hirundo-neoxena> bird:account "A swallow with glossy blue-black upperparts, a rust-red face and throat and a deeply forked tail. It is a common bird of open country in southern Australia. It arrived in New Zealand on its own in the 1950s and spread quickly. It builds a cup of mud under bridges and the eaves of buildings."@en ;
