<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/icthyophaga-vocifer> bird:account "A large eagle with a white head, breast and tail, chestnut belly and black wings. It sits on trees by lakes and rivers south of the Sahara and catches fish from the surface. Its loud, ringing call is a symbol of African wetlands. It is the national bird of Zambia, Zimbabwe, Namibia and South Sudan."@en ;
