<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/malurus-cyaneus> bird:account "A tiny bird with a long, cocked tail. In the breeding season the male has a bright blue crown, cheeks and back. It lives in groups with a dominant pair and helpers. Although pairs are socially bonded, many chicks are fathered by males from other groups, and males show yellow petals to females outside their group."@en ;
