<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/milvus-milvus> bird:account "A graceful bird of prey with a deeply forked rufous tail and long, angled wings. It eats carrion, worms and small mammals. Persecution made it extinct in England and Scotland, but reintroduction since 1989 has made it common again over the Chiltern Hills and other areas."@en ;
