<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/neophema-chrysogaster> bird:account "A small grass parrot with a bright green back, a yellow belly with an orange patch and a blue band on the forehead. It breeds only at Melaleuca in south-west Tasmania and crosses Bass Strait each autumn to winter on the salt marshes of Victoria and South Australia. Only a few dozen birds remain in the wild."@en ;
