<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/nestor-meridionalis> bird:account "A forest parrot, olive-brown with crimson under the wings and on the belly. It moves noisily through the canopy in small groups, and feeds on fruit, nectar, seeds, sap and grubs dug from wood. Introduced predators reduced it to offshore islands and large forests, but fenced sanctuaries in Wellington and elsewhere have brought it back to cities."@en ;
