<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/nestor-notabilis> bird:account "A large olive-green parrot of the Southern Alps, with orange-red under the wings. It is the only alpine parrot in the world. Kea are bold and curious: they investigate cars, packs and huts, and solve puzzles in captivity. The diet includes roots, berries, insects and carrion. Its loud call, a long 'kee-aa', gives the bird its name."@en ;
