<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/passer-montanus> bird:account "A small sparrow with a chestnut crown and a black spot on each white cheek. Males and females look alike. In much of East Asia it is the common sparrow of towns and villages. In Europe it lives on farmland and at the edge of woodland, and its numbers fell sharply in the late twentieth century."@en ;
