<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/pelecanus-conspicillatus> bird:account "A very large black and white pelican with the longest bill of any bird. Flocks fish together by herding fish into shallow water. When rain fills the inland salt lakes, tens of thousands of pelicans fly hundreds of kilometres to breed on their islands, then leave as the water dries."@en ;
