<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/phoeniconaias-minor> bird:account "The smallest and most numerous flamingo, deep pink, with a dark red bill. It filters blue-green algae from the surface of soda lakes. Flocks of more than a million birds gather at lakes of the East African Rift, such as Lake Nakuru and Lake Bogoria. Most birds breed at Lake Natron in Tanzania."@en ;
