<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/platalea-minor> bird:account "A white spoonbill with a black face and a black, spoon-shaped bill that it sweeps from side to side through shallow water to catch fish and shrimp. It breeds on rocky islets off the west coast of Korea and in north-eastern China, and winters in Taiwan, Hong Kong, Japan and Vietnam. Annual counts have risen from a few hundred birds to several thousand."@en ;
