<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/ploceus-capensis> bird:account "A large yellow weaver of south-western South Africa. The male has an orange face in the breeding season and weaves a hanging nest of grass with a downward entrance tube. A male builds several nests in a season and shows each one to females, which inspect it before they accept it."@en ;
