<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/porphyrio-hochstetteri> bird:account "A large, flightless rail with deep blue and green plumage and a heavy red bill. It grazes on tussock bases and fern rhizomes in alpine grassland. It was thought extinct until its rediscovery in the Murchison Mountains of Fiordland in 1948. Today birds live in Fiordland, at sanctuaries and on predator-free islands."@en ;
