<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/prosthemadera-novaeseelandiae> bird:account "A dark honeyeater that shines green and blue in sunlight, with two white tufts at the throat. It sings a complex song of bells, clicks, wheezes and notes too high for people to hear, and it can mimic other birds. It feeds on nectar of flax, kōwhai and pūriri, and defends flowering trees against other birds."@en ;
