<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/rhipidura-albiscapa> bird:account "A small grey flycatcher with a long tail that it fans while it hunts insects in flight. It has white eyebrows, a white throat and white edges to the tail. It lives in forests, woodlands and gardens across Australia. It was once treated as the same species as the New Zealand fantail, so many older Australian records carry the name Rhipidura fuliginosa."@en ;
