<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/selasphorus-rufus> bird:account "A small, fiery orange hummingbird. It breeds further north than any other hummingbird, up to southern Alaska. Its migration is one of the longest of any bird relative to body size: a round trip of about 6,000 km between Alaska and Mexico, following the flowering of plants along the mountains."@en ;
