<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/turdus-merula> bird:account "A thrush of woods and gardens. The male is black with an orange-yellow bill and eye-ring, and the female is dark brown. Its rich, fluting song is heard at dawn and dusk from rooftops. It was introduced to New Zealand and Australia in the nineteenth century, and is now common there."@en ;
