<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/vultur-gryphus> bird:account "One of the largest flying birds, with a wingspan of more than three metres. It is black with a white collar and white patches on the wings. The male has a fleshy comb. It soars along the Andes and the coasts of Chile and Argentina, seldom flaps its wings, and feeds on carrion."@en ;
